'''''Syzygium myrtifolium''''', the '''red lip''' or '''kelat oil''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Myrtaceae]].<ref name="nparks_3156" >{{cite web |url=https://www.nparks.gov.sg/florafaunaweb/flora/3/1/3156 |title=''Syzygium myrtifolium'' (Roxb.) Walp. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=19 August 2022 |website=nparks.gov.sg |publisher=Flora Fauna Web |access-date=5 July 2024 |quote=Common Name: Kelat Oil, Kelat Paya, Red Lip, 红楠木 }}</ref> It is native to Bangladesh, Myanmar, Thailand, [[Peninsular Malaysia]], [[Sumatra]], [[Java]], [[Borneo]], and the Philippines.<ref name="POWO_60445221-2" >{{cite POWO |id=60445221-2 |title=''Syzygium myrtifolium'' Walp. |access-date=5 July 2024 }}</ref> A shrub or dense tree from {{cvt|2|to|20|m|ft|0}} tall, it is typically found in coastal areas, lowlands, and other wet tropical situations.<ref name="nparks_3156" /> It has found use as a garden, street, and landscaping shrub or tree, due to its colorful young leaves, amenability to pruning (including [[topiary]]), and fragrant flowers.<ref name="nparks_3156" /><ref name="UTP_Sm" >{{cite web |url=https://tropical.theferns.info/viewtropical.php?id=Syzygium+myrtifolium |title=Useful Tropical Plants ''Syzygium myrtifolium'' |last1=Fern |first1=Ken |date=20 July 2022 |website=tropical.theferns.info |publisher=Tropical Plants Database |access-date=5 July 2024 }}</ref>
